meta {
  name: Verify OTP
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/auth/verify-otp
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "phone": "{{client_phone}}",
    "code": "108905"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    bru.setVar("client_token", res.body.token);
  }
}

docs {
  # Verify OTP

  Verifies the OTP. Auto-registers the client on first login.
  Returns a Sanctum token named `mobile-client`.
  The script saves it to `client_token`.

  Rate limited: 10/min per IP, 5/min per phone.
  After **5 failed** attempts the cached OTP is discarded.

  Blocked clients (`is_blocked`) get **403** and do not receive a token.
  Blocking a client also revokes existing Sanctum tokens.

  Token lifetime: `SANCTUM_TOKEN_EXPIRATION` minutes (default 30 days).

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "token": "1|...",
    "is_new": true,
    "client": {
      "id": 1,
      "name": null,
      "phone": "+99361111222"
    }
  }
  ```

  Use `is_new: true` to open the profile setup screen.

  **Errors:**
  - `403` — client account is blocked
  - `422` — invalid or expired OTP
  - `429` — too many requests
}
